cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Judge the Judge: a clinician-validated mini-study of LLM judges for AI-generated clinical notes"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Mensah
    given-names: Paulina
date-released: 2026-10-29
version: "1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Boadiwaa/judge-the-judge"
url: "https://judge-the-judge.fly.dev"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  24 synthetic UK consultations, 72 AI-style notes and 174 planted documentation errors with a
  clinician-reviewed risk-graded answer key, used to measure how many errors three LLM judge designs
  (naive, rubric, claim-by-claim checking) detect, with confidence intervals. The code is MIT-licensed;
  the dataset is CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - clinical documentation
  - ambient AI scribe
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - patient safety
  - evaluation
